</section>
<section id="Sx4.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Ablation Analysis</h3>

<div id="Sx4.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To rigorously demonstrate the effectiveness of our two-stage pipeline, we quantitatively compare the baseline (default manual configuration), after Task-to-MDP Mapping (Stage 1), and after subsequent Algorithmic Optimization (Stage 2). As summarized in Figure <a href="#Sx4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Ablation Analysis ‣ Experiments ‣ Agent²: An Agent-Generates-Agent Framework for Reinforcement Learning Automation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, most environments and algorithms show clear improvements: Task-to-MDP Mapping improves performance in 83% of scenarios, and Algorithmic Optimization delivers additional gains in 67% of cases.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After Stage 1, In Ant-v4 with TD3, the average episode reward jumps from 3853.8 (baseline) to 5981.4, an impressive 55% improvement.
In the challenging SMAC-1c3s5z scenario, the win rate increases from 0.17 to 0.21 (a 25% relative gain), and in MetaDrive with SAC, the reward rises from 178.2 to 219.6 (a 23% increase).
For most environments, Task-to-MDP Mapping alone enables the agent to outperform the baseline by a large margin, demonstrating the effectiveness of automatic MDP adaptation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Second, Algorithmic Optimization further boosts performance, especially in more challenging tasks or with sensitive algorithms. For instance, in Ant-v4 with PPO, Stage 2 brings an additional 13% improvement over Stage 1 (3831.9 vs. 3385.4). In Humanoid-v4 with SAC, performance improves by another 11.6% after Stage 2 (6787.9 vs. 6081.2). Similarly, in MetaDrive with SAC, the reward increases by an additional 18% (259.8 vs. 219.6), and in SMAC-1c3s5z, the win rate continues to climb from 0.21 to 0.23 (a further 10% relative gain).</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These findings highlight the complementary nature of our pipeline: Task-to-MDP Mapping accurately constructs a specialized training MDP from natural language task descriptions, enabling rapid adaptation of the agent to the environment structure, while Algorithmic Optimization fine-tunes learning for maximum effectiveness.
Together, these stages enable robust and fully automated generation of high-performing RL agents across a diverse range of single-agent and multi-agent benchmarks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.13368v1/improvement_comparison.png" id="Sx4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/352;" width="698" height="352" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Performance improvement comparison across Task-to-MDP Mapping and Algorithmic Optimization.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Sx5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Conclusion</h2>

<div id="Sx5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we present Agent<sup id="Sx5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup>, a fully automated, LLM-driven agent-generates-agent framework that significantly advances the automation, accessibility, and performance of RL development. By introducing a novel dual-agent architecture and a two-stage pipeline that separates MDP modeling from algorithmic optimization, Agent<sup id="Sx5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> is able to autonomously translate high-level task descriptions and raw environment code into high-performing RL agents—entirely without human intervention.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Extensive experiments across single-agent and multi-agent benchmarks demonstrate that Agent<sup id="Sx5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> consistently outperforms manually designed baselines, achieving performance improvements across all evaluated environments and algorithms, which validates both the effectiveness and generality of the proposed approach.
Our ablation analysis further highlights the complementary impact of automated environment adaptation and iterative algorithmic refinement.
Notably, Agent<sup id="Sx5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> achieves performance improvement in 83% of task-algorithm pairs after automated MDP adaptation, and a further gain in 67% of cases following algorithmic optimization.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Ultimately, Agent<sup id="Sx5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_sup">2</sup> establishes a new paradigm in which intelligent agents can autonomously design, optimize, and deploy other agents, thereby breaking through traditional barriers of RL development and setting the stage for the next generation of automated AI systems.</p>
</div>
</section>
